  "ui_text": "AEGIS Search Geodata Settings Start new chat History Show conversation history How is the air quality in Milan right now? Air quality in Milan right now Based on the latest Open-Meteo air-quality data for central Milan (45.464, 9.190), retrieved 2026-10-01 10:50 UTC (12:50 local, Europe/Rome): Pollutant Current value Unit PM10 ~27.5 µg/m³ PM2.5 ~20.7 µg/m³ Nitrogen dioxide (NO₂) ~22.1 µg/m³ Ozone (O₃) ~78.0 µg/m³ Overall: Moderate. PM2.5 is the main concern — at roughly 21 µg/m³ it sits above the WHO 24-hour guideline (15 µg/m³) but below the EU daily limit (25 µg/m³). PM10 and NO₂ are in a moderate range; ozone is moderate-to-elevated for the afternoon. Trend over the next 24 hours: Pollution builds overnight. PM10 climbs from ~27 µg/m³ this afternoon to a peak of ~46 µg/m³ around 09:00 on Oct 2, and PM2.5 rises from ~21 to ~38 µg/m³ over the same period. NO₂ also spikes in the evening (up to ~66 µg/m³ around 21:00) before easing. Ozone follows the opposite pattern, dropping overnight and recovering tomorrow afternoon. So conditions are likely to worsen tonight into tomorrow morning. Notes and caveats: This is a point forecast for the city center; it does not capture street-level or neighborhood variation across Milan. The data is a modeled forecast product, not a live monitoring-station reading, so treat the \"current\" values as the nearest forecast hour rather than a measured observation. Values are reported in µg/m³ as provided by the source. If you'd like, I can map this for Milan or pull a specific pollutant or time window. Send message Context Unavailable Ready for a location or data request Hide chat Alerts MAP WORKSPACE Ask for a location or map data to load the workspace. Agent model Needs attention Satellite Available Optional Keys Optional Tool activity Needs attention",
